 handle←type CreateHandle content;new;pool
⍝ Create a "drawing" object handle from source namespace contents
⍝ Note: Use standardized "content" names as much as possible (e.g. Type, Props, Uses)
⍝? Should this be renamed to NewPool (or somesuch) and moved to the framework tool list? Only if we're going to need this for something else, outside of Draw.

 :If 0=##.GUIroot.⎕NC'_Pool' ⋄ '_Pool'##.GUIroot.⎕NS'' ⋄ :EndIf ⋄ pool←##.GUIroot._Pool ⍝ Find where we keep global handles (creating it if necessary)
 new←⎕VGET(pool⍕⍛,'.',##.Next pool)⎕NS(Type:type)content ⍝ Build our new handle namespace with the next-available name
 handle←⊃2⊃⎕VFI 1↓##.LeafName⍕new ⍝ Return them the global handle # for them to use later
 ⍝ These handle namespaces can just be erased when no longer needed, but if they point to any special content (such as external storage or EWC objects)
 ⍝ then those may need to be separately cleaned up before erasure.
